# Netlify redirects — Zero Lines
#
# This site is static HTML. Every route below exists as a real file, so there is
# no SPA to fall back for.
#
# The previous version ended with a catch-all rewrite:
#     /*    /index.html    200
# which meant Netlify never served 404.html. Every mistyped or dead URL returned
# the homepage with HTTP 200 — a soft 404. Google treats those as duplicate
# content and they hide broken links from any crawler or monitoring. Removed:
# Netlify serves /404.html automatically for unmatched paths.

# --- Legacy hash-router URLs from the pre-clean-URL SPA -----------------------
# Hash fragments are never sent to the server, so these cannot be redirected
# server-side; zl.js rewrites them client-side on load. Listed here as a record.

# --- Trailing slashes ---------------------------------------------------------
# Netlify serves directory routes WITH a trailing slash and 301s /science to
# /science/ itself. Declaring the reverse here created two rules pointing in
# opposite directions — dormant today because Netlify's own handling wins, but a
# redirect loop waiting to happen. Canonicals now use the trailing-slash form
# that is actually served, and no rule is needed.

# --- Convenience aliases ------------------------------------------------------
/journal                    /blog/                    301
/faq                        /faq.html                 301
/privacy                    /privacy.html             301
/terms                      /terms.html               301
/cookies                    /cookies.html             301
/accessibility              /accessibility.html       301
/shipping                   /shipping-returns.html    301
/shipping-returns           /shipping-returns.html    301
# These two pointed at /#analyser — a homepage anchor that does not exist — so
# anyone typing zerolines.life/analyser landed at the top of the homepage and
# never found the analyser at all. They now go to the page itself.
/analyser                   /analyser/                301
/analyzer                   /analyser/                301
